{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>וַאֲכַלְתֶּם בְּשַׂר בְּנֵיכֶם וְגוֹ׳ תֹּאכֵלוּ.</b> The reason He repeated to say ״תֹּאכֵלוּ״ a second time is to say that even after they have already eaten, their compassion will not be stirred in the usual way — to be consoled after the deed and to have their compassion stirred and to weep ״woe, my son, woe, my daughter״ — but rather they will again agree to eat if they find any of them anew." "<b>Or</b> it may intend that they will rush to eat the sons first, and the reason is that since they have set their eyes to eat the daughters as well, therefore they will rush to eat the sons first, because there is concern that the sons might refuse and flee when they see the daughters being eaten — something one need not worry about regarding the daughters, for they do not have the strength of the males. And this is what the verse says: <b>וַאֲכַלְתֶּם בְּשַׂר בְּנֵיכֶם</b>. And the reason for prioritizing the sons and not the daughters is not that you have no intention to eat the daughters, but rather that you will additionally also eat the flesh of your daughters, and you prioritize the sons because there is a concern for a felt reason." "<b>Or</b> it may say along these lines: since a father's compassion for sons is greater than for daughters (Shabbat 66b), therefore they scheme to eat the sons first, so that through this it will become easier for them to eat the daughters. And this is the measurement of the verse: <b>וַאֲכַלְתֶּם בְּשַׂר בְּנֵיכֶם</b>, and the reason it was prioritized is so that <b>שֶׁבְּשַׂר בְּנוֹתֵיכֶם תֹּאכֵלוּ</b> — meaning, your heart will not ache in accordance with what preceded, and it will be to you like ordinary food:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:24.050014479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}